<title>HONG KONG: China Eastern surges on active buying.</title>
<headline>China Eastern surges on active buying.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in China Eastern Airlines Corp Ltd rose sharply following a buy recommendation by Salomon Brothers, brokers said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Shares of the Chinese flag-carrier jumped to a record of HK$1.93 before retreating slightly to close at HK$1.87, up HK$0.16 or 9.4 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;Chinese investors are seen snapping the stock at prices of between HK$1.86 to HK$1.90,&quot; a broker at a regional house said.</p>
<p>Salomon forecast that the airline's earnings could grow close to 20 percent in the fiscal year 1998.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6369</p>
